---
import Base from "../layouts/Base.astro";
---

<Base
  title="Privacy Policy"
  description="PostPigeon Privacy Policy — how we collect, use, and protect your data."
>
  <div class="prose-page">
    <h1>Privacy Policy</h1>
    <p class="meta">Effective date: 25 March 2026 &nbsp;·&nbsp; Last updated: 25 March 2026</p>

    <p>
      PostPigeon ("we", "us", or "our") is committed to protecting your privacy.
      This policy explains what information we collect, how we use it, and your rights
      regarding that information.
    </p>

    <h2>1. Information we collect</h2>
    <p>
      We collect only the minimum information needed to provide the service:
    </p>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>Email address</strong> — collected when you join the waitlist or create an account.</li>
      <li><strong>Usage data</strong> — basic, anonymised telemetry (page views, feature interactions) to help us improve the product. No personal identifiers are attached.</li>
      <li><strong>Content you create</strong> — posts, images, and scheduling data you enter into the dashboard. This data is stored solely to deliver the service back to you.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>2. How we use your information</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>To send you a single notification email when early access opens (waitlist only).</li>
      <li>To operate and maintain the PostPigeon service.</li>
      <li>To diagnose errors and improve reliability.</li>
      <li>To comply with legal obligations.</li>
    </ul>
    <p>We do <strong>not</strong> sell, rent, or share your personal data with third parties for marketing purposes.</p>

    <h2>3. Data storage &amp; security</h2>
    <p>
      Your content and credentials are stored in your own infrastructure when you
      self-host PostPigeon. For cloud-hosted plans (when available), data is stored in
      encrypted databases. We use industry-standard TLS for data in transit and
      AES-256 encryption for data at rest.
    </p>
    <p>
      Platform API credentials (OAuth tokens, API keys) are stored only in your
      environment and are never transmitted to or stored on PostPigeon servers.
    </p>

    <h2>4. Cookies &amp; tracking</h2>
    <p>
      The public landing page uses no third-party tracking cookies. We may set a
      single first-party session cookie for authentication purposes when you log in
      to the dashboard. We do not use advertising cookies or fingerprinting.
    </p>

    <h2>5. Third-party services</h2>
    <p>
      PostPigeon integrates with third-party platforms (X/Twitter, LinkedIn, Threads,
      Reddit, Dev.to, GitHub) on your behalf. Your use of those platforms is governed by
      their respective privacy policies. We only access the scopes you explicitly authorise.
    </p>

    <h2>6. Data retention</h2>
    <p>
      Waitlist emails are retained until early access launches, after which they are
      deleted unless you create an account. You may request deletion at any time by
      emailing <a href="mailto:privacy@postpigeon.app">privacy@postpigeon.app</a>.
    </p>
    <p>
      Account data is retained for the lifetime of your account and deleted within 30 days
      of account closure.
    </p>

    <h2>7. Your rights</h2>
    <p>Depending on your jurisdiction, you may have the right to:</p>
    <ul>
      <li>Access the personal data we hold about you.</li>
      <li>Request correction of inaccurate data.</li>
      <li>Request deletion of your data ("right to be forgotten").</li>
      <li>Object to or restrict processing.</li>
      <li>Data portability.</li>
    </ul>
    <p>
      To exercise any of these rights, contact us at
      <a href="mailto:privacy@postpigeon.app">privacy@postpigeon.app</a>.
    </p>

    <h2>8. Children's privacy</h2>
    <p>
      PostPigeon is not directed at children under 13. We do not knowingly collect
      personal data from children. If you believe we have inadvertently collected such
      data, please contact us immediately.
    </p>

    <h2>9. Changes to this policy</h2>
    <p>
      We may update this policy periodically. Material changes will be communicated via
      email if you are on the waitlist or registered as a user. The "Last updated" date
      at the top of this page will always reflect the current version.
    </p>

    <h2>10. Contact</h2>
    <p>
      Questions? Email us at
      <a href="mailto:privacy@postpigeon.app">privacy@postpigeon.app</a>.
    </p>
  </div>
</Base>
